In article <1f.7651.1682.0NC5BB23@compart.fi>, riku.saikkonen@compart.fi (Riku Saikkonen) writes:
>What are the possible places of a portal to Fort Ludios (knox)?
>
>I looked at the source... A level below 10, above the medusa level,
>having a vault and not another level branch. BUT, I've looked at every
>level below 10 (up to 22, the medusa level), broke into every vault (not
>so hard in Wizard mode) (on levels above 10 too) and no portal!
>
>Hmm... Does the portal not appear in every game?
>
No. Actually the game generates the Ludios portal in a following way:
- generate level.
- if the level has a vault, and it has no other portals, is not a special
  level and is in main dungeon below level 10 but above medusa, and the 
  Ludios portal has not been generated yet then
- generate Ludios portal with 1/3 probability.

So it is quite difficult to compute the probability of having a Ludios 
portal in your game - you need the probability of getting a vault on a 
level fulfiling all the cryteria above... I would estimate that an average
game has about 3-4 levels fulfiling the cryteria. That would mean about
20-30% probability of NOT having the portal.

>The ^O in Wizard mode displays Fort Ludios as 19 and knox also as 19.
>And a 'floating branch' to Fort Ludios.
>
>So, where is the portal?
>
It has not been generated. Otherwise you'd get a level number attached to your
'floating branch'. 

